is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the HTTP service (Apache2) on the internal server srv1, which also hosts internal DNS.

Mechanism: Name resolution was functioning, but the web service itself was down. On client PCs, DNS resolved srv1.jeremysitlab.com to 10.5.0.4 (evidence: pc1/pc2/pc3 getent returned “10.5.0.4 srv1.jeremysitlab.com” and ping to the name succeeded). However, initial web fetches failed because there was no HTTP listener on srv1 (evidence: on srv1, apache2.service was “inactive (dead)” and ss showed “NO_HTTP_LISTEN” for :80/:443). This presents to non-technical users as “site can’t be found,” even though DNS was up; the browser simply couldn’t reach a web server at the resolved address.

Localization: srv1 (10.5.0.4)
